    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1007">

                <pb facs="0876" n="864" sameAs="frus:frus1940v05/pg864"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">611.2231/444: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Minister in Ecuador</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Long</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1940-06-04T12:00:00-04:00">June 4, 1940—noon</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>58. Your 83, May 31, 7 p.m. You may inform the Foreign Minister that we are
                    willing to consider May 9 as the date of formal notice by <pb facs="0877"
                        n="865" xml:id="pg865"/> the Ecuadoran Government under the currency clause
                    of Article VII of the agreement; likewise, that the manner and extent of the
                    proposed restrictions on schedule products, which would of course apply to
                    imports of the affected products from all countries, appear in substance to be
                    satisfactory.</p>
                <p>More detailed instructions cannot be sent until we receive your despatch
                        1046.<anchor n="48" xml:id="d1007-f1"/> It is hoped that it may be possible
                    to conclude arrangements so as to permit the imposition of restrictions
                    beginning June 10.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
